{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7STJfq5jzr9etFJKMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WvEy2GfBf5SsYDLuRoxRa4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"^- \\`menu\\.\\|new E.Menu\\|^- \\`talk\\.\\|game.settings\\|settings\\.\\|game.menu\\|^- \\`input\\.\\(use\\|bind\\|actions\\|map\\)\\|anyPressed\\|hover\" API-INDEX.md | head -70","description":"Grep API index for menu, dialog, settings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5375,"cache_read_input_tokens":89921,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5375,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"d4ab3aee-8624-4a65-aa44-e57630b419c1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:17:00.349Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7SSurbymp3cdDHAAFT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WvEy2GfBf5SsYDLuRoxRa4":{"command":"grep -n \"^- \\`menu\\.\\|new E.Menu\\|^- \\`talk\\.\\|game.settings\\|settings\\.\\|game.menu\\|^- \\`input\\.\\(use\\|bind\\|actions\\|map\\)\\|anyPressed\\|hover\" API-INDEX.md | head -70","description":"Grep API index for menu, dialog, settings"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvEy2GfBf5SsYDLuRoxRa4","type":"tool_result","content":"261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixels a device pixel apart in size) or 'auto' (fill on high-density screens, phones and tablets, where that difference can't be seen; sharp elsewhere). game.settings.scale sets it\n276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n277:- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel)\n330:- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, on top of the game's zoom), and noted at the top of the screen ('ZOOM 1.65x': the number a scene's camera.start takes). Does nothing where the scene doesn't let the player zoom. Returns the zoom\n521:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the updates still run every refresh). The player's Frame rate setting (game.settings.frameRate: 'auto', '60', 'full') can fix it at 2 or 1\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n576:- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"7784da33-ad9a-4799-8cc3-58b4181d50b6","timestamp":"2026-1