{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfA3VysA8XbGDnYRgFjD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WokAbU6BJCbXEKqDzUcCze","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK'\"); b=s.index(\"  ['CREDITS'\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\n    'Issues caught: 11 (hub ready() lost to a scene-change timer, touch-only gate never showing, keys outside the bindings not ending the demo, Enter both choosing a card and skipping the creative meeting, a pitch you could win with one card, the projector screen out of frame, overlapping prompts, an overflowing objection box, a name label left over dialog, a bad material name, a busy floor).',\n    'Critical / game breaking: 2 (the AI Hub round never starting; touch-only devices getting a menu they could not use).',\n    'Most helpful: the AI Hub harness in automatic mode, and a scripted headless play-through of a whole day with screenshots.',\n    'Least helpful: the 24-device viewport matrix of the title screen: every one came back clean.']],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    'Liked most: shapes as data (the whole mid-century office is a few lines per desk), the Dialog box with live portraits, and coroutine scripts on game time for the pitch.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: game.after() timers are cleared by game.go(), so a ready() call scheduled with it never fired; input.lastDevice starts as keyboard, so it cannot tell a touch-only device.',\n    'Built myself: the pitch card battle with its delivery and closer meters, the PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs, the attract-mode bot, the AI Hub ghost layer.',\n    'Hardest: the pixel font has no PlayStation shape glyphs, so every prompt needed hand-drawn buttons.',\n    'Overhaul: the single-step pressed() for keys bound to two actions (Enter is both start and confirm).',\n    'Change: a built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for the last device.']],\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\n    'Liked: the freedom to pick the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching instead of a shooter.',\n    'Confusing: the multiplayer line asks for AI Hub integration and multiplayer for the game on its own; local hot seat was my reading of the second.',\n    'Hardest: fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub and a three-day story into one vertical slice.',\n    'One more test: a real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet, to judge text size and glyphs.']],\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs; cat > ../exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-02 18:13\",\n    \"source\": \"Mad Men (2007-2015), the AMC television drama created by Matthew Weiner\",\n    \"genre\": \"Narrative adventure / office life sim with a card-and-timing pitch battle\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter top-down (engine threequarter view), switchable to isometric and top-down in the office\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine from the handoff package), plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol 1); bundled into one HTML file with a small Node script\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art: PS1-era resolution, shaded HD Humanoid rigs, furniture as data shapes, canvas lighting, in a mid-century palette of walnut, teal, mustard and orange\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (walk cycles, idle breathing, poses, expressions, live dialog portraits) plus engine scripts and tweens\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-written jazz loops on the engine chip synth (title, office bossa, pitch, closer, evening ballad, win and lose stings), synthesized sound effects, and Simlish gibberish voices pitched per character\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1-4 players: seeded deal, shared positions shown as ghosts, progress and results); local 2-player hot-seat Pitch-Off offline\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless Chromium via Playwright (scripted play-throughs, faked DualSense gamepad), WebKit iPhone emulation for the touch-only gate, AI Hub harness automatic runs (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; host-leave), viewport-matrix across 24 device/engine combinations; no real phone, real controller or real iOS Safari\",\n    \"research\": \"None online beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation; the source drawn from general knowledge\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"11 issues: AIHub.ready() never sent because a game.after() timer was cleared by the scene change; the touch-only gate never showed; keys outside the bindings did not end the attract demo; Enter both chose a card and skipped the creative meeting; the pitch could be won with one card; the projector screen was out of frame; prompts overlapped; the objection box overflowed; a name label stayed over dialog; a bad material name; floors too busy.\",\n    \"2 critical: the AI Hub round never starting (ready never sent), and touch-only devices getting a menu they could not use.\",\n    \"The AI Hub harness in automatic mode, closely followed by a scripted headless play-through of a whole day with screenshots at every stage.\",\n    \"The viewport-matrix run of the title screen across 24 devices: all clean, it found nothing.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Shapes as data (a whole 1964 office from a few lines per desk), the Dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts on game time, which made the pitch sequence easy to write.\",\n    \"Yes: game.after() timers are cleared by game.go(), so a ready() scheduled that way never fired; and input.lastDevice defaults to keyboard, so it cannot be used to detect a touch-only device. Also Enter is bound to both start and confirm, which caused a double action.\",\n    \"The pitch system: the card battle against objections, the delivery timing meter, the hold-and-release closer with projector slides, plus the attract-mode bot and the AI Hub ghost layer.\",\n    \"Controller prompts: input.label() returns PlayStation symbols the pixel font cannot draw, so every button glyph had to be hand drawn.\",\n    \"The overlapping default bindings of the menu actions (Enter as both start and confirm, Escape as both pause and cancel).\",\n    \"A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph (PlayStation shapes, Xbox letters, key caps, mouse) for the last device used.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The freedom to choose the genre, which let Mad Men become a game about talking, drinking and pitching rather than a forced action game.\",\n    \"The multiplayer line: AI Hub integration plus multiplayer for the game on its own was ambiguous; I read the second as local hot seat.\",\n    \"Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story with endings into one polished vertical slice.\",\n    \"A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet, to judge text size, glyphs and pacing as the prompt intends.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Mad Mention\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Win the room. Hold the pause.\",\n    \"description\": \"Walk a 1964 Madison Avenue agency gathering ideas before two o'clock, then pitch them to the client: answer each objection with the right appeal and deliver your tagline on the beat.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Adventure\",\n    \"source\": \"Mad Men\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD walk, Cross/E talk, Triangle/Tab ideas, Square/V view; in the pitch pick an idea and press on the gold\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"story\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('ok',len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"; ls -la ..; pkill -f \"http.server 38694\"","description":"Finalize about text, build, write and validate exit interview"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":344804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":882,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"0b65ef95-9dcf-48d5-87f3-50d5a1539284","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:51:32.103Z","request_id":"req_011CgfA3VWb8nqTRP3yQgedY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WokAbU6BJCbXEKqDzUcCze":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK'\"); b=s.index(\"  ['CREDITS'\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\n    'Issues caught: 11 (hub ready() lost to a scene-change timer, touch-only gate never showing, keys outside the bindings not ending the demo, Enter both choosing a card and skipping the creative meeting, a pitch you could win with one card, the projector screen out of frame, overlapping prompts, an overflowing objection box, a name label left over dialog, a bad material name, a busy floor).',\n    'Critical / game breaking: 2 (the AI Hub round never starting; touch-only devices getting a menu they could not use).',\n    'Most helpful: the AI Hub harness in automatic mode, and a scripted headless play-through of a whole day with screenshots.',\n    'Least helpful: the 24-device viewport matrix of the title screen: every one came back clean.']],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    'Liked most: shapes as data (the whole mid-century office is a few lines per desk), the Dialog box with live portraits, and coroutine scripts on gam