losely followed by a scripted headless play-through of a whole day with screenshots at every stage.\",\n    \"The viewport-matrix run of the title screen across 24 devices: all clean, it found nothing.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Shapes as data (a whole 1964 office from a few lines per desk), the Dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts on game time, which made the pitch sequence easy to write.\",\n    \"Yes: game.after() timers are cleared by game.go(), so a ready() scheduled that way never fired; and input.lastDevice defaults to keyboard, so it cannot be used to detect a touch-only device. Also Enter is bound to both start and confirm, which caused a double action.\",\n    \"The pitch system: the card battle against objections, the delivery timing meter, the hold-and-release closer with projector slides, plus the attract-mode bot and the AI Hub ghost layer.\",\n    \"Controller prompts: input.label() returns PlayStation symbols the pixel font cannot draw, so every button glyph had to be hand drawn.\",\n    \"The overlapping default bindings of the menu actions (Enter as both start and confirm, Escape as both pause and cancel).\",\n    \"A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph (PlayStation shapes, Xbox letters, key caps, mouse) for the last device used.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The freedom to choose the genre, which let Mad Men become a game about talking, drinking and pitching rather than a forced action game.\",\n    \"The multiplayer line: AI Hub integration plus multiplayer for the game on its own was ambiguous; I read the second as local hot seat.\",\n    \"Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story with endings into one polished vertical slice.\",\n    \"A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet, to judge text size, glyphs and pacing as the prompt intends.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Mad Mention\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Win the room. Hold the pause.\",\n    \"description\": \"Walk a 1964 Madison Avenue agency gathering ideas before two o'clock, then pitch them to the client: answer each objection with the right appeal and deliver your tagline on the beat.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Adventure\",\n    \"source\": \"Mad Men\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD walk, Cross/E talk, Triangle/Tab ideas, Square/V view; in the pitch pick an idea and press on the gold\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"story\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('ok',len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"; ls -la ..; pkill -f \"http.server 38694\"","description":"Finalize about text, build, write and validate exit interview"}}}
