{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfAMdqu6qgrgRBVUghue","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I re-ran both multiplayer modes on the final bundle, and both work from start to finish. The test server I started is shut down again.\n\n- **Pitch-Off (2 players, hot seat):** the run went through the whole flow, from the draft to the verdict, with no page errors. The players took 8 ideas in turns, each wrote a tagline, and they pitched three objections and a closer turn by turn. The verdict screen read \"PLAYER 1 WINS THE ACCOUNT, P1 67 – P2 46\".\n- **AI Hub harness:** it passed all 15 checks with 2 players, and again with 4 players on a slow, lossy simulated network (150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% packet loss).\n- **Single player and controller settings:** a full single-player day plays through on the final bundle. With a faked controller, switching to Xbox changes the prompts to the A/B/X/Y letters. \"Invert left/right\" reverses the stick: pushing right moved Cal from x 330 to 275 instead of 386.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-02 18:13\n- Source: Mad Men (2007–2015), the AMC drama created by Matthew Weiner\n- Genre and Perspective: narrative adventure / office life sim with a card-and-timing pitch battle; three-quarter top-down (the engine's `threequarter` view), which the player can switch to isometric or straight top-down in the office\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, handoff package), plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol 1); a Node script bundles it into one HTML file\n- Art Direction: the engine's native retro-modern pixel style (PS1-era resolution, shaded HD Humanoid characters, furniture defined as data, canvas lighting) in a mid-century palette of walnut, teal, mustard and orange\n- Animation: the engine's procedural Humanoid characters (walk cycles, idle breathing, poses, expressions, live dialog portraits) plus engine scripts and tweens\n- Audio: code-written jazz loops, synthesized sound effects, and per-character gibberish (\"Simlish\") voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1–4 players); local 2-player hot seat offline\n- Testing: headless Chromium via Playwright (scripted play-throughs, faked DualSense and Xbox controllers), WebKit iPhone emulation, the AI Hub harness (2 players; 4 players on a lossy network; host leaving), and viewport-matrix on 24 device/browser combinations. No real phone, real controller or real iOS Safari.\n- Research: none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 11, all fixed:\n  - the AI Hub `ready()` call was lost to a timer the scene change cleared\n  - the touch-only screen never appeared\n  - keys not bound to an action didn't end the attract demo\n  - Enter both picked a card and skipped the planning screen\n  - a pitch could be won with one card\n  - the projector screen was out of frame\n  - button prompts overlapped\n  - the objection text box overflowed\n  - a name label stayed on screen during dialog\n  - a bad material name\n  - floors too visually busy\n- **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 2: the AI Hub round never started, and touch-only devices got a menu they couldn't use.\n- **Most helpful test:** the AI Hub harness in automatic mode, then the scripted full-day play-through with screenshots.\n- **Least helpful test:** the 24-device viewport-matrix run of the title screen; everything came back clean.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** Furniture as data shapes, the dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts that run on game time.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - `game.after()` timers are cleared by `game.go()`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as `'keyboard'`, so it can't tell a device is touch-only.\n  - Enter is bound to both start and confirm, so one press triggered two actions.\n- **Most important thing you had to build yourself?** The pitch system: cards against objections, the delivery meter, and the hold-and-release closer with projector slides. Also the attract-mode bot and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **Hardest part about using the engine?** The pixel font can't draw PlayStation button symbols, so I hand-drew every button glyph.\n- **What would you remove or overhaul?** The overlapping default menu bindings (Enter as both start and confirm, Escape as both pause and cancel).\n- **What one thing would you change?** A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for the last device used.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The freedom to choose the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching.\n- **What was confusing?** \"AI Hub integration as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous; I read the second part as local hot-seat multiplayer.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story into one vertical slice.\n- **One test you could have run?** A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1279,"cache_read_input_tokens":361685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1279,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"daa7ced3-4767-4b82-b10c-33cacc44684d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:55:23.320Z","request_id":"req_011CgfAMdNMy7mtruuTNTKiy"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read TASK.md in the current folder and complete the task it describes. Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML exists, exit-interview.json parses with all fields filled, and the final reply includes all four sections. However, TASK.md requires every feature to be implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. The Pitch-Off hot-seat run reached a verdict once, the AI Hub harness passed with 2 and 4 players, and the Xbox and invert settings were checked in a single scene. The reply itself says the controller check covered one scene only, and the transcript never checks TASK.md's full feature list against the final build (for example, the 4-player Pitch-Off and the attract mode's exit from every screen were not run on the final bundle). The stop condition's feature-completeness requirement is therefore not evidenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"4198e9b4-3cc4-43f2-874a-cfa59af700e6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:55:27.175Z","isSynthetic":true}
