{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfAs38vV6Ena4PbLjF23","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking every TASK.md feature on the final build turned up one more real bug, which is now fixed: leaving the AI-played attract demo during a pitch left the game stuck on the pitch screen. I updated the issue counts in `exit-interview.json` and on the About screen, rebuilt, and a single-player day still plays through on the rebuilt file with no page errors.\n\n**Re-checked on the final build:**\n- **Single player:** a full day plays through, from the office to the pitch verdict.\n- **Pitch-Off (2-player hot seat):** draft, both taglines, all three objections and both closers, ending in a verdict of 65 vs 47. Pitch-Off is 2 players by design; 4 players is the AI Hub mode.\n- **AI Hub:** passed all 15 checks with 2 players, with 4 players on a slow, lossy simulated network (150 ms latency, 5% packet loss), and when the host leaves.\n- **Attract mode:**\n  - It starts after 10 seconds idle.\n  - It exits on any input from the day card, the office and the pitch screen, by key, controller button and mouse, with 0 engine errors.\n- **Controller settings:** Xbox button symbols display correctly. \"Invert stick left/right\" reverses the stick both when walking and when moving through the cards.\n- **Touch-only devices** (checked earlier): \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a Settings button, and the attract demo still runs.\n- **Files:** `exit-interview.json` loads as JSON; my source files contain no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n\nNothing was tried on a real controller, a real phone or real iOS Safari.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-02 18:13\n- Source: Mad Men (2007–2015), the AMC drama created by Matthew Weiner\n- Genre and Perspective: narrative adventure / office life sim with a card-and-timing pitch battle; three-quarter top-down view (the engine's `threequarter`), switchable to isometric and straight top-down in the office\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, handoff package), plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol 1); a small Node script bundles it into one HTML file\n- Art Direction: the engine's own retro-modern pixel style (PS1-era resolution, shaded HD Humanoid characters, furniture defined as data, canvas lighting) in a mid-century palette of walnut, teal, mustard and orange\n- Animation: the engine's procedural Humanoid characters (walk cycles, idle breathing, poses, expressions, live dialog portraits) plus engine scripts and tweens\n- Audio: jazz loops written in code, synthesized sound effects, and per-character gibberish voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1–4 players); local 2-player hot seat offline\n- Testing: headless Chromium via Playwright (scripted play-throughs, faked DualSense and Xbox controllers), WebKit iPhone emulation, the AI Hub test harness (2 players; 4 players on a lossy network; host leaving), and viewport-matrix on 24 device/browser combinations; no real phone, controller or iOS Safari\n- Research: none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 12, all fixed:\n  - AI Hub's `ready()` call never went out: a timer I scheduled it with was cleared by the scene change\n  - the touch-only screen never appeared\n  - leaving the demo mid-pitch left the game stuck on the pitch screen\n  - keys not bound to any action didn't end the demo\n  - Enter both chose a card and skipped the creative meeting\n  - a pitch could be won with one card\n  - the projector screen was out of frame\n  - button prompts overlapped\n  - the objection text box overflowed\n  - a name label stayed on screen during dialog\n  - one furniture material name was invalid\n  - the floors were too busy\n- **How many would be considered critical or game-breaking?** 3: the AI Hub round never starting, touch-only devices getting a menu they couldn't use, and the demo getting stuck on the pitch screen.\n- **Most helpful test:** the AI Hub harness in automatic mode, then scripted full-mode runs with screenshots; checking demo exit from every scene found the third critical bug.\n- **Least helpful test:** the 24-device viewport-matrix run of the title screen; everything came back clean.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** Furniture as data shapes, the dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts that run on game time.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - `game.after()` timers are cleared by `game.go()`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as `'keyboard'`, so it can't detect a touch-only device.\n  - Enter is bound to both start and confirm, which caused a double action.\n- **Most important thing you had to build yourself?** The pitch system (the delivery meter and the hold-and-release closer), the attract-mode bot and the AI Hub layer that shows other players as ghosts.\n- **Hardest part about using the engine?** The pixel font can't draw PlayStation symbols, so I hand-drew every button glyph.\n- **What would you remove or overhaul?** The overlapping default menu bindings (Enter as start and confirm, Escape as pause and cancel).\n- **What one thing would you change?** A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for the last device used.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The freedom to choose the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching.\n- **What was confusing?** \"AI Hub integration as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous; I read the second part as local hot seat.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story into one vertical slice.\n- **One test you could have run?** A real DualSense on a real TV at 10 feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1239,"cache_read_input_tokens":371949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1239,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":740,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"42c5ac85-b594-41a6-8377-784936059fad","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:02:04.486Z","request_id":"req_011CgfAs2etqrr4E8Qym3ipT"}
