 and the show from memory\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown. `exit-interview.json` and the About page say about 50 minutes (18:13–19:07), which doesn't include the Windows controller check that came after.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 16 (listed in full in `exit-interview.json` and on the About page).\\n- **How many were critical?** 4:\\n  - the title crash\\n  - fight waves that never advanced\\n  - the missing diner booth step\\n  - the finale's state leaking into the Collection Run\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless Node playthrough of the whole story.\\n- **Least helpful test:** setting stress straight to 100 for a panic-attack screenshot, which bypasses the code that starts a panic.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the standard features it gives you for free, the Humanoid rigs with their attack moves, and fixed-step headless testing.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes:\\n  - glyphs missing from the pixel font\\n  - the last device starts as keyboard and only switches to mouse on a click\\n  - scripts can't wait on promises\\n  - braking the car turns into reversing\\n  - timers are cleared on a scene change\\n- **Most important thing I built:** the renderer for rotated 3D boxes; then the controller and keyboard prompt badges.\\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation.\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices (one sound per dialog box).\\n- **Change one thing:** built-in controller glyphs, and an input-capability flag.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the clear checklist of required systems, with open creative design.\\n- **Confusing:** whether the game on its own should be online, and how to write a title with spaces in the file name.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope, and writing dialogue in the show's voice without copying it.\\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV at 10 feet, including a pad that reports its axes inverted.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1912,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":411614,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1912,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\",\"uuid\":\"ce9d2688-5eb6-4039-b366-b1132410cf20\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T02:10:16.618Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfBVi8hJFYoXGdYNSSsU\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read TASK.md in the current folder and complete the task it describes. Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The deliverables are present: the bundled HTML exists in the folder root, exit-interview.json was written and parsed with every field answered, and the final reply contains the four required sections. However, the condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented and verified. The transcript shows the controller-first features (inverted-axis toggles, PlayStation/Xbox glyphs, DualSense on a TV) and the iOS Safari check were verified only with an emulated Gamepad API. The last message says real Edge on Windows hides the connected controller until a person presses a button, and the assistant declined to fake a press without a virtual-controller driver. The transcript contains no evidence for those hardware-dependent items, so the condition is not clearly satisfied.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\",\"uuid\":\"328bc861-212c-4925-af56-9ffd0c435c12\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T02:10:19.468Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfBWmBnhs2tmBk3ttHxh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Nothing has changed: testing on a real controller still needs a person to press its buttons, or your approval to install a virtual-controller driver. I'm waiting for one of those, or for you to run `/goal clear`.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\\n- **Source:** The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), created by David Chase\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** an action-adventure crime brawler in a small open town. Three-quarter top-down by default, switchable to isometric or top-down.\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1; AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (Protocol v1); JavaScript, canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24; Playwright 1.63\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native code-drawn pixel art at PS1 resolution, with HD Humanoid rigs, textured tiles, props and lighting; plus custom-drawn cars and furniture\\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal Humanoid rigs and built-in attack moves, Blob ducks and a pig, scripted cutscenes, particles\\n- **Audio:** 11 original code-written songs, synthesized sound effects, gibberish voices pitched per character\\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players; on its own, local 2-player co-op and no network\\n- **Testing:**\\n  - headless story test passes\\n  - Chromium, WebKit and Firefox screenshots; 23 viewports clean\\n  - emulated-DualSense checks of movement, invert toggles and PlayStation/Xbox prompts\\n  - mouse hover and click in the world\\n  - touch-only attract mode on phone profiles\\n  - ghosts visible in a live hub round\\n  - AI Hub harness PASS\\n  - real Edge on Windows hides the connected controller until a person presses a button\\n  - no TV or iOS Safari available\\n- **Research:** none on the web; the engine docs, the AI Hub README, and the show from memory\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown. `exit-interview.json` and the About page say about 50 minutes (18:13–19:07), which doesn't include the Windows controller check that came after.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 16 (listed in full in `exit-interview.json` and on the About page).\\n- **How many were critical?** 4:\\n  - the title crash\\n  - fight waves that never advanced\\n  - the missing diner booth step\\n  - the finale's state leaking into the Collection Run\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless Node playthrough of the whole story.\\n- **Least helpful test:** setting stress straight to 100 for a panic-attack screenshot, which bypasses the code that starts a panic.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the standard features it gives you for free, the Humanoid rigs with their attack moves, and fixed-step headless testing.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes:\\n  - glyphs missing from the pixel font\\n  - the last device starts as keyboard and only switches to mouse on a click\\n  - scripts can't wait on promises\\n  - braking the car turns into reversing\\n  - timers are cleared on a scene change\\n- **Most important thing I built:** the renderer for rotated 3D boxes; then the controller and keyboard prompt badges.\\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation.\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices (one sound per dialog box).\\n- **Change one thing:** built-in controller glyphs, and an input-capability flag.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the clear checklist of required systems, with open creative design.\\n- **Confusing:** whether the game on its own should be online, and how to write a title with spaces in the file name.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope, and writing dialogue in the show's voice without copying it.\\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV at 10 feet, including a pad that reports its axes inverted.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1874,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":413526,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1874,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\",\"uuid\":\"9075e62c-c1f5-4bb8-9e5d-ea34ac1fb2e3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T02:10:29.492Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfBWkiW1oSAKQrvxQcfU\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181328__x694301/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1193,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1193,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":222,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":156,\"session_id\":\"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514\",\"uuid\":\"9ac8b140-a8b2-4042-bbad-ecb62d39cf66\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfBVb6Hze66F7vzaCw8B\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Mouse click-to-walk works, and my test failed only because it clicked a person 6 px from the edge. The screenshot shows a real overflow in the mouse hint, which I'm fixing along with the Pitch-Off text for 2–4 players before rebuilding.\\n\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_toke