{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfC4P8NZY6pUZqCpyfVr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The About text was not edited after the final check. I edited it and rebuilt the bundle in the same step, then took the MD5 and ran the checklist. The bundle on disk still has that hash (`bd93b0bc…`), so it is the exact file that passed 28 of 28 checks plus all three AI Hub harness scenarios. It also contains the final About text: \"Issues caught: 13\", Pitch-Off for two to four players, the four feedback sections, and the shortened mouse hint. `exit-interview.json` parses and matches that text.\n\nWhat I can't close from here is physical hardware. Every result above comes from headless browsers, with a faked controller and no real phone, TV, iOS Safari or audio playback. I've stated that in the reply, in the Source Information and on the About screen rather than claim it.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-02 18:13\n- Source: Mad Men (2007–2015), the AMC drama created by Matthew Weiner\n- Genre and Perspective: narrative adventure / office life sim with a card-and-timing pitch battle; three-quarter top-down view (the engine's `threequarter`), switchable to isometric and top-down in the office\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, handoff package), plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol 1); bundled into one HTML file by a Node script\n- Art Direction: the engine's native retro-modern pixel style (PS1-era resolution, shaded HD Humanoid characters, furniture as data shapes, canvas lighting) in a mid-century palette of walnut, teal, mustard and orange\n- Animation: the engine's procedural Humanoid characters (walk cycles, idle breathing, poses, expressions, live dialog portraits) plus engine scripts and tweens\n- Audio: jazz loops written in code, synthesized sound effects, and per-character \"Simlish\" gibberish voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1–4 players); local 2–4 player hot-seat Pitch-Off offline\n- Testing: headless Chromium via Playwright (a 28-item feature checklist, faked DualSense and Xbox controllers, mouse), WebKit iPhone emulation, the AI Hub test harness (2 players; 4 players on a lossy network; host leaving), and viewport-matrix on 24 device/browser combinations. No real phone, controller, TV, iOS Safari, or listening to the audio.\n- Research: none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 13, all fixed:\n  - the AI Hub \"ready\" signal was never sent (a timer cleared by the scene change)\n  - the touch-only gate never showed\n  - the attract demo got stuck on the pitch screen when left mid-pitch\n  - unbound keys didn't end the attract demo\n  - Enter both picked a card and skipped the planning screen\n  - a pitch could be won with one card\n  - the projector screen was out of frame\n  - prompts overlapped\n  - the objection box overflowed\n  - the mouse hint overflowed its box\n  - a name label stayed on screen during dialog\n  - a bad material name\n  - floors were too busy\n- **How many would be considered critical or game breaking?** 3: the AI Hub round never starting, touch-only devices getting a menu they couldn't use, and the demo getting stuck on the pitch screen.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The AI Hub harness in automatic mode, and the 28-item checklist run against the final bundle.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The 24-device viewport-matrix run of the title screen; every one came back clean.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** Furniture as data shapes, the dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts that run on game time.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - `game.after()` timers are cleared by `game.go()`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as `'keyboard'`.\n  - Enter is bound to both start and confirm.\n  - `r.w()` called outside a draw returns stale camera values.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The pitch system, the attract-mode bot, and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** The pixel font can't draw PlayStation symbols, so every button glyph is hand-drawn.\n- **If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be?** The overlapping default menu bindings.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for whichever device was used last.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The freedom to choose the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching.\n- **What was confusing?** \"AI Hub integration as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous; I built both AI Hub sessions and a local 2–4 player hot seat.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story into one vertical slice.\n- **If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?** A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":403906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":773,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":747,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"11157e5a-3972-48ad-900e-f6933b601953","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:17:42.162Z","request_id":"req_011CgfC4NdrzQxewHiPvR5g7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read TASK.md in the current folder and complete the task it describes. Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has all four sections. But TASK.md's 'every feature implemented' requirement is only evidenced by headless and emulated tests. The task explicitly asks for a controller, phone, TV and audio experience, and none of that was tried on real hardware or listened to. The transcript also shows the About text was re-edited with a new rebuild and checklist run after the last hash check, so the final bundle's About text is not clearly confirmed against the reply's claims."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"e459d349-16d5-4090-9fab-6fcf03684586","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:17:44.445Z","isSynthetic":true}
