rish voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1–4 players); local 2–4 player hot-seat Pitch-Off offline\n- Testing: headless Chromium via Playwright (the 28-item feature checklist, simulated DualSense and Xbox controllers, the mouse, an audio signal measurement), WebKit iPhone emulation, the AI Hub test page (2 players; 4 players on a lossy network; the host leaving), and viewport-matrix on 24 device/browser combinations. Nothing on a real phone, controller, TV or iOS Safari, and the audio has not been listened to.\n- Research: none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 13, all fixed:\n  - the AI Hub ready signal was never sent\n  - the touch-only screen never showed\n  - the attract demo got stuck on the pitch screen when left mid-pitch\n  - keys with no action bound didn't end the attract demo\n  - Enter both picked a card and skipped the creative meeting\n  - a pitch could be won with one card\n  - the projector screen was out of frame\n  - on-screen prompts overlapped\n  - the objection box overflowed\n  - the mouse hint overflowed its box\n  - a name label stayed on screen during dialog\n  - one material name was invalid\n  - floors were too busy\n- **How many would be considered critical / game-breaking?** 3: the AI Hub round never starting, touch-only devices getting a menu they couldn't use, and the demo stuck on the pitch screen.\n- **Most helpful test:** the AI Hub test page in automatic mode, and the 28-item checklist run against the final bundle.\n- **Least helpful test:** the 24-device viewport-matrix run of the title screen; every one came back clean.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** Furniture defined as data shapes, the dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts on game time.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - `game.after()` timers are cleared by `game.go()`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as `'keyboard'`.\n  - Enter is bound to both start and confirm.\n  - `r.w()` called outside a draw returns stale camera values.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The pitch system, the attract-mode bot, and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** The pixel font can't draw the PlayStation button symbols, so every button glyph is hand-drawn.\n- **If you had to remove or overhaul one thing, what would it be?** The overlapping default menu bindings.\n- **If you could change one thing, what would it be?** A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for whichever device was used last.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The freedom to choose the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching.\n- **What was confusing?** \"AI Hub integration as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous; I built both AI Hub sessions and a local 2–4 player hot seat.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story into one vertical slice.\n- **If there was one test you could have run, what would it be?** A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2471,"cache_read_input_tokens":410714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2471,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"4a2efc60-1409-4eea-8577-ba6d02253993","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:19:00.252Z","request_id":"req_011CgfC9yzFgEp