{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfCFCbBAaAeoKvkUXYRG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have nothing left that can close this gap. The hook asks for play on a real controller, TV and phone and for listening to the audio, and none of that hardware exists on this machine. I won't say it was done, because it wasn't. More browser runs wouldn't change that.\n\nEvery feature TASK.md lists is built into the final bundle (hash `bd93b0bc…`). That exact file passed my 28-item feature checklist and all three AI Hub harness scenarios. `exit-interview.json` loads as valid JSON with every field answered, and the source has no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n\nThe remaining step is for someone to play it once on a DualSense and a TV and on a phone, with the sound on. If you're happy to treat that as follow-up, `/goal clear` will end this loop.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-02 18:13\n- Source: Mad Men (2007–2015), the AMC drama created by Matthew Weiner\n- Genre and Perspective: narrative adventure / office life sim with a card-and-timing pitch battle; three-quarter top-down view (the engine's `threequarter`), switchable to isometric and top-down in the office\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, handoff package), plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol 1); bundled into one HTML file by a Node script\n- Art Direction: the engine's own retro-modern pixel style (PS1-era resolution, shaded HD Humanoid characters, furniture defined as data shapes, canvas lighting) in a mid-century palette of walnut, teal, mustard and orange\n- Animation: the engine's procedural Humanoid characters (walk cycles, idle breathing, poses, expressions, live dialog portraits) plus engine scripts and tweens\n- Audio: code-written jazz loops, synthesized sound effects, and per-character Simlish gibberish voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode (1–4 players); local 2–4 player hot-seat Pitch-Off offline\n- Testing:\n  - headless Chromium via Playwright: the 28-item feature checklist, faked DualSense and Xbox pads, mouse, and an audio signal measurement\n  - WebKit iPhone emulation\n  - AI Hub harness: 2 players; 4 players on a lossy network; the host leaving\n  - viewport-matrix on 24 device and browser combinations\n  - no real phone, controller, TV or iOS Safari, and the audio was not listened to\n- Research: none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 13, all fixed.\n- **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 3: the AI Hub round never started, touch-only devices got a menu they couldn't use, and the attract demo got stuck on the pitch screen when you left it.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The AI Hub harness in automatic mode, and the 28-item checklist on the final bundle.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The 24-device viewport-matrix run of the title screen; every one came back clean.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** Furniture defined as data shapes, the dialog box with live portraits and choices, and coroutine scripts on game time.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - `game.after()` timers are cleared by `game.go()`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as `'keyboard'`.\n  - Enter is bound to both start and confirm.\n  - `r.w()` called outside a draw returns stale camera values.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The pitch system, the attract-mode bot, and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** The pixel font can't draw PlayStation symbols, so every button glyph is hand-drawn.\n- **If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be?** The overlapping default menu bindings.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A built-in prompt widget that draws the right glyph for the last device used.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The freedom to choose the genre, so Mad Men could be a game about talking and pitching.\n- **What was confusing?** \"AI Hub integration as well as for the game on its own\" was ambiguous; I built both AI Hub sessions and a local 2–4 player hot seat.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting attract mode, local versus, AI Hub sessions and a three-day story into one vertical slice.\n- **If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?** A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":420444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2013,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd4161a-5598-4ff8-9e94-bd9d9c377514","uuid":"2c9e5bea-dfb6-4169-8307-775e97788191","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:20:08.121Z","request_id":"req_011CgfCFC89bHAYC2Das57cq"}
